# CASES below copies each case's RUN lines from its .test or .mlir file until that
# case's switch commit deletes them there; until then, edit both copies.
"""The CTNative lit cases with no pytest test in a driver or in a deeper
cases.py (Checks, Fixtures, Lowering and PartialEvaluation have their own), as
pytest tests: test_case is parametrized over CASES, whose keys are the cases'
lit paths relative to this folder without .test or .mlir, so
`test_case[Browser/page/dom-reads]` is lit's `ctcompile ::
CTNative/Browser/page/dom-reads.test`. Each test runs all of its case's RUN
lines in order through lit_lines.run, every line under bash, as lit runs them.
"""

